# Files Vercel does not need for the static client deploy.
#
# EVERY pattern is anchored to the repo root with a leading "/". That is not
# cosmetic: an un-anchored name matches at ANY depth (gitignore semantics), so
# a bare `tools` line also dropped src/tools/ — which
# src/client/NatureDressing.js imports — and a bare `textures` line dropped
# assets/props/*/textures (the glTF textures). The deployed client then died
# with "Failed to load the game code" because its module graph 404'd.
#
# test/deploy.test.mjs enforces the anchoring, so this cannot regress.
/node_modules
/data
/test
/tools
/docs
/.github
/cloudflared
/Dockerfile
/docker-compose.yml
/playwright-report
/*.log
/*.md
/textures
